174
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:04,650
Oh.

175
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:31,700
I heard that it ran out of power
and no damage was starting.

176
00:10:34,660 --> 00:10:39,740
Regardless, I imagine its very existence
was shocking to the scientists of the time.

177
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:42,257
It's extraordinary.

178
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:44,900
Beyond any technology in its era.

179
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:49,257
Hundreds of years later, I'd say
this is still quite the shock.

180
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:53,869
They were trying to wake it up, but it
might be better if it stays like this.

181
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:56,040
It could be dangerous.

182
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:59,637
No one knows where this iron
giant came from, after all.

183
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:03,485
It's unclear what it was trying
to do or what it was capable of.

184
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:08,357
As for the world government, predictably
they ordered its destruction.

185
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:11,700
But the scientists of
that age protected it.

186
00:11:12,020 --> 00:11:14,760
They hid it away where
no one could find it.

187
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:17,620
And to this day, no one knows it is here.

188
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:20,280
Not even the government itself.

189
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,180
Anyway, I'm surprised you
made it to this junkyard.

190
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:30,320
