259
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,030
What?

260
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:36,600
Rob Lucci?

261
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:41,460
I guess it's time to feed the cat. Huh?

262
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:44,237
Oh, and look, we've got
five tuna steaks here.

263
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:46,732
Come on, let's hand these goofballs over.

264
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:51,617
Let me out of these shoes
right now, you sick bastard!

265
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:52,530
No!

266
00:14:52,613 --> 00:14:53,443
Why is he here?

267
00:14:53,526 --> 00:14:55,120
I thought he quit his job!

268
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:56,912
We can't let him get in!

269
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:58,880
You better not even try!

270
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:00,986
I'll send him packing myself!

271
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:03,217
Don't worry, Robin, you're safe with us.

272
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:05,517
We'll beat him as many times as it takes.

273
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:06,430
Thank you.

274
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:09,364
Officially, they're here
to return the seraphim.

275
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:12,760
Tell them to leave it and
send them away. Excuse me?

276
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:15,617
We're going to bar the government's entry.

277
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:16,935
Lock down the island!

278
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,660
Wait, stop!

279
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:36,357
You're still under repair!

280
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:38,028
You can't start moving now!

281
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:45,940
Dragon, help!

282
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:48,240
There's something wrong with Kuma!

283
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:49,440
Huh? Kuma?

284
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:51,920
Stop, Kuma! What happened?

285
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:56,521
Maybe the Navy is still
giving him orders somehow!

286
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,880
What do you need?

287
00:16:06,060 --> 00:16:07,001
Let us help you!

288
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:10,120
Can you at least tell us
where you're trying to go?

289
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:20,380
What started this? I don't know!

290
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:21,997
He just got up out of the blue!

291
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,727
He's not supposed to
have any free will left!

292
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:27,837
Kuma! Stop it!

293
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,508
You're gonna hurt yourself!

294
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:32,160
Come back here, Kuma!

295
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,536
Where are you going?

296
00:16:40,740 --> 00:16:42,180
Kuma! Kuma!

297
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:47,680
We need you, Kuma!

298
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,257
You're part of our family!

299
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:52,458
We have to stick together
and see our battle through!

300
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:00,620
No, Goomba, stop!

301
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,160
Please, don't go!

302
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:11,940
He's gone.

303
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:19,537
Thank you for returning
our seraphim to us.

304
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:22,677
Unfortunately, your request
for entry is denied!

305
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:24,837
So just drop him off and go please.

306
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:30,137
Uh, Noni Dory S Bear can return
home on his own from there.

307
00:17:30,220 --> 00:17:34,097
He'll have to forgive us but we are
so busy we can barely think straight.

308
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:36,920
So um, order S Bear to

309
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:38,937
return, and you can call it a day.

310
00:17:39,020 --> 00:17:39,957
Mission complete.

311
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:41,057
Thank you for your service.

312
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:42,375
Whoa there, you can't

313
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,417
just leave us out in the cold.

314
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:46,029
Seems they're wrong to us.

315
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:48,497
Aren't you at least going to
invite us in for a cup of tea?

316
00:17:48,580 --> 00:17:49,877
We've been sailing for days.

317
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:51,237
We're freezing out here.

318
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:55,057
Naval Branch G-14 is
right around the corner.

319
00:17:55,140 --> 00:17:57,317
I'm sure they'll welcome
you with open arms.

320
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,700
Am I speaking to Vegapunk? Yes.

321
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:01,900
I have a question for you, Doctor.

322
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:05,560
What do you know about the
Egghead disappearances?

323
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:09,622
Disappearances?

324
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:10,960
I beg your pardon?

325
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:12,929
I'm afraid I don't follow.

326
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:15,700
Two months ago, Cipher Pole No.

327
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:17,920
5's ship vanished into thin air.

328
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:20,580
A month ago, it was Cipher Pole No. 7.

329
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:23,260
Two weeks ago, Cipher Pole No. 8.

330
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:26,640
Quite the strange coincidence. In fact,

331
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:28,637
not one government ship that has visited

332
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:31,117
Egghead in the past two
months has returned.

333
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:34,553
I was hoping you might be able
to shed some light on why.

334
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:42,797
Well, I am so sorry to hear that, but
rest assured we don't have them here.

335
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:46,645
My records show that all vessels
have shipped out in ship shape!

336
00:18:47,380 --> 00:18:49,460
Hey, what exactly are you implying?

337
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:53,577
Are you trying to say we've been messing
with those ships, you overgrown house cat?

338
00:18:53,660 --> 00:18:54,600
Go to hell!

339
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:57,697
Lilith, I know you're evil, but
please don't antagonize him?

340
00:18:57,780 --> 00:19:01,780
You are going to look so stupid
when I open this port! Lilith, no!

341
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:02,977
Back up, Pythagoras!

342
00:19:03,060 --> 00:19:06,397
Ah, well, my gosh, there's no ship
here, but we appreciate your visit.

343
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:07,310
Goodbye.

344
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:10,600
Fine, then, if you insist. Go.

345
00:19:12,620 --> 00:19:15,267
Nice try, but I doubt
they're going to budge.

346
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:16,948
Shall we move on to plan B?

347
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,220
Everyone, get ready.

348
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:22,047
We're going to abandon ship.

349
00:19:23,780 --> 00:19:25,140
We'll use the Seraphim.

350
00:19:25,280 --> 00:19:26,657
Hesper follows our orders.

351
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:28,975
We'll have it transport us to Egghead.

352
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:32,317
We're sacrificing the ship.

353
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:36,120
As soon as we leave it will fall
prey to the sea beast weapons

354
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:42,753
That's a tad bit risky, don't you think?

355
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:45,937
Impatience isn't attractive
in a man, you know?

356
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:50,640
If you want to be swallowed by the sea,
you're welcome to stay and threats to!

357
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:52,510
Let's go

358
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:10,480
You want to leave this place, old man?

359
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:11,820
But it's your lab.

360
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:13,617
I thought you liked living here.

361
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:15,060
What's not to like?

362
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:18,020
Why, I'm creating the future itself here.

363
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:22,200
I can use government facilities
and funds however I please.

364
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:26,220
And thus, my research has
continued at an extraordinary pace.

365
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:29,080
You've seen only a small
fraction of my work.

366
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:35,020
My brain is a fountain of
ideas that never stops flowing.

367
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:38,200
But there's not enough
time, not enough help,

368
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:41,780
not enough money to make
my true dream a reality.

369
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:45,537
You mean you're planning
something even bigger?

370
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:47,267
You want to know what it is?

371
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:49,460
You probably do!

372
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:53,440
When it happens, the whole
universe will know my name.

373
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:56,960
Oh, is it another big robot?

374
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:58,297
Tell us, please!

375
00:20:58,380 --> 00:21:00,040
Very well, then.

376
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:01,791
It's really quite simple.

377
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:04,253
I will use science to squash inequality.

378
00:21:04,520 --> 00:21:08,860
I will create a world where
free energy is provided to all!

379
00:21:10,860 --> 00:21:14,060
That's not the reaction
I expected. I don't know.

380
00:21:14,300 --> 00:21:15,877
Free stuff's cool, I guess.

381
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:18,617
That would be a worthwhile
endeavor if you could achieve it.

382
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:20,641
Most wars are fought over energy.

383
00:21:20,880 --> 00:21:24,617
We might be able to achieve world
peace, but resources are too limited.

384
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,080
Are they limited?

385
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:28,440
Or is it mankind who is limited?

386
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,520
Energy is everywhere.

387
00:21:32,700 --> 00:21:37,540
You can feel it in the air, in
the ground, it's all around us.

388
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:40,240
It's simply overflowing.

389
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:43,120
The world is full of energy.

390
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:49,940
All we need to do is convert
it into tangible power.

391
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:52,937
Inequality will become
a thing of the past.

392
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:55,460
Wars will come to an end.

393
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:02,620
With the power of science, we
can make this world a utopia.

394
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,680
Still not interested?

395
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:11,797
No, I think it's really cool that
you want to make people happy.

396
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:14,080
But hero stuff just isn't my thing.

397
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:17,137
Anyway, you never said
why you want to leave.

398
00:22:17,220 --> 00:22:18,677
Well, I have a problem.

399
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:23,500
The more I try to create this energy,
the further I delve into lost history.

400
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:25,280
For example,

401
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:28,817
I can't help but to look to our
giant mechanical friend here

402
00:22:28,900 --> 00:22:32,700
and wonder what kind of ancient
energy source powered him.

403
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:36,500
It is the nature of a scientist
to remain curious after all.

404
00:22:36,780 --> 00:22:41,880
So I took a little peek into history
and unraveled some forbidden truths.

405
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:48,180
I was only carrying on my friend's will,
but it took me deep into dangerous waters.

406
00:22:58,600 --> 00:22:59,977
And that's my story.

407
00:23:00,060 --> 00:23:01,737
I just left learning too much.

408
00:23:01,820 --> 00:23:03,517
Now the government will erase me.

409
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:05,100
Just like Aura.

410
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:07,857
This can't be good.

411
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:09,457
It must be CP0.

412
00:23:09,540 --> 00:23:11,000
Wait, Zero?

413
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:15,917
They're a spy organization directly under
the orders of the Celestial Dragons.

414
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,597
I thought they were called CP9.

415
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:19,739
Did they change their name or what?

416
00:23:20,260 --> 00:23:21,760
CP0 is a higher rank.

417
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:24,280
You rarely see them make a move.

418
00:23:24,600 --> 00:23:28,894
But when they do, it means that the
course of history is about to change.

419
00:23:30,740 --> 00:23:33,140
This place is incredible!

420
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:35,797
Why, I've never seen anything like it!

421
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:39,056
It's unreal, like we stepped
straight into the future!

422
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:41,319
I'm getting a little fired up here.

423
00:23:42,120 --> 00:23:43,777
What's Cypherpole doing here?

424
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:45,837
And why aren't they
wearing their black suits?

425
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:46,840
How bizarre.

426
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:49,717
Don't they usually come
in through the port?

427
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:50,660
Hey, guys!

428
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:55,537
We just got a report that two of the Sea
Beast weapons were attacked at the shore!

429
00:23:55,620 --> 00:23:56,520
Don't tell me.

430
00:23:56,740 --> 00:23:58,377
Does that mean...

431
00:23:58,460 --> 00:23:59,720
they're intruders?

432
00:24:04,500 --> 00:24:06,340
Shaka, CP0 is on the island.

433
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:10,320
We're too late! They're here!

434
00:24:10,940 --> 00:24:12,897
Luchi's being a giant pain in the ass.

435
00:24:12,980 --> 00:24:14,737
What else is new, cat bastard?

436
00:24:14,820 --> 00:24:16,120
Come on!

437
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:17,960
Give it up already, Luchi!

438
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:23,800
I'm still stuck!

439
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:26,737
Would you fix these stupid
future shoes already?

440
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:28,580
I need my damn feet!

441
00:24:28,780 --> 00:24:30,604
How else can I keep Robin safe?

442
00:24:31,600 --> 00:24:33,718
How did they come ashore so quickly?

443
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:47,460
Well, definitely not by ship.

444
00:24:47,680 --> 00:24:48,915
That's for darn sure.

445
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:51,517
Seems they realized the
Sea Beast weapons would

446
00:24:51,600 --> 00:24:54,117
attack their ship as soon
as they refused to leave.

447
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:57,788
They must have used the
Seraphim's Papa power to fly here.

448
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:59,059
What should we do?

449
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:00,580
How resourceful.

450
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:04,744
They must really want to fight if
they're sacrificing their ship.

451
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:05,790
Very well.

452
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:07,460
If that's what you desire.

453
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:09,181
Sound the alarm!

454
00:25:09,380 --> 00:25:11,321
We need to evacuate the citizens!

455
00:25:11,600 --> 00:25:12,460
Roger that!

456
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:25,842
Tell Atlas to return to the lab.

457
00:25:26,940 --> 00:25:29,234
Prepare all of the Seraphim for combat.

458
00:25:30,500 --> 00:25:31,971
Sentomaru will lead them.

459
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:42,880
Releasing Seraphim number one.

460
00:25:43,580 --> 00:25:44,460
S .Hawk.

461
00:25:50,820 --> 00:25:53,420
Releasing Seraphim, number three, S-Snake.

462
00:25:58,880 --> 00:26:01,480
Releasing Seraphim, number four, S-Shark.

463
00:26:05,340 --> 00:26:06,170
Deploy!

464
00:26:09,060 --> 00:26:12,237
If the world government has
decided they want to kill me,

465
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:14,261
then I don't have much time left.

466
00:26:15,120 --> 00:26:17,920
CP0 is here, so I need to pack my bags.

467
00:26:18,180 --> 00:26:22,420
Now please honor my requaser
and take me out to sea with you.

468
00:26:22,940 --> 00:26:26,077
You make it sound like we're all
just going on a picnic or something.

469
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:28,320
If you disappear, it'll be big news.

470
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:31,461
This might put an even
bigger target on our backs.

471
00:26:33,100 --> 00:26:35,453
Okay, your head looks funny, so why not?

472
00:26:35,580 --> 00:26:36,660
Is that a reason?

473
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:39,870
Splendid.

474
00:26:39,953 --> 00:26:41,737
Somehow I had a feeling you'd say yes.

475
00:26:41,820 --> 00:26:43,820
All right, let us go.

476
00:26:44,260 --> 00:26:46,240
This will be a battlefield soon.

477
00:26:46,700 --> 00:26:50,700
For starters, please bring Bonnie
to the Lobby face above the clouds.

478
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:52,353
How do we get up there?

479
00:26:52,560 --> 00:26:53,900
It should be easy.

480
00:26:54,180 --> 00:26:55,717
Just take the vacuum rocket.

481
00:26:55,800 --> 00:26:58,447
You can find it down
here in the Fabrio face.

482
00:26:58,660 --> 00:27:00,120
What's a vacuum rocket?

483
00:27:00,220 --> 00:27:01,220
That sounds cool!

484
00:27:01,900 --> 00:27:03,740
Well, don't dawdle now, boys.

485
00:27:04,180 --> 00:27:06,651
See you in the sky in the blink of an eye.

486
00:27:09,160 --> 00:27:10,197
He disappeared!

487
00:27:10,280 --> 00:27:12,900
You're awesome, Mr. Appelman!

488
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:16,240
I'm finding the future
to be very confusing.

489
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:19,540
Hey, take a gander at that.

490
00:27:19,780 --> 00:27:21,600
It's a giant monster!

491
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:35,420
Damn it!

492
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:36,600
It won't die!

493
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:39,205
The force go right through it!

494
00:27:39,620 --> 00:27:41,100
Of course they do.

495
00:27:41,300 --> 00:27:45,077
This island is full of technical
marvels beyond your wildest imagination.

496
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:48,395
If you think your guns will
work here, you've been had.

497
00:27:48,980 --> 00:27:51,717
I've always wanted to
fight something like you.

498
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:53,420
Something untouchable.

499
00:27:54,140 --> 00:27:56,400
And I know why they couldn't hurt you.

500
00:27:56,760 --> 00:27:58,780
Because you're from outer space!

501
00:28:01,720 --> 00:28:04,360
Prepare yourself, alien fiend!

502
00:28:19,820 --> 00:28:22,920
It must have some sort
of space physiology.

503
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:24,340
It's no use.

504
00:28:24,620 --> 00:28:26,777
I'm not giving up. Well, you should.

505
00:28:26,860 --> 00:28:27,880
It's a hologram.

506
00:28:28,160 --> 00:28:29,877
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

507
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:31,960
Have you perhaps been here before?

508
00:28:32,300 --> 00:28:33,920
Let's say it's nostalgic.

509
00:28:35,440 --> 00:28:36,997
Well, I'm already up here.

510
00:28:37,080 --> 00:28:40,962
I might as well check out whatever
this thing is above the clouds.

511
00:28:41,060 --> 00:28:43,648
Chances are that's where
Vegapunk is hiding.

512
00:28:44,060 --> 00:28:48,354
Tell me, Luchi, do you see those yellow
lines way up there in the clouds?

513
00:28:48,780 --> 00:28:49,610
Yes.

514
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:54,367
Watch what happens when
someone crosses them.

515
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:04,520
Laser beams automatically fire on them.

516
00:29:08,780 --> 00:29:11,662
It's a defensive system
called the Frontier Dome.

517
00:29:11,760 --> 00:29:14,995
It encircles the labophase,
guarding in all directions.

518
00:29:18,380 --> 00:29:22,556
The lesson here is not to underestimate
the world's greatest scientist.

519
